  "problem": "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=\u27e83\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t)-5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3t)+2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\u27e9,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$\n\n$v=\u27e8${{field-1}}$\\,,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-12\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3t)\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t)-5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3t)+2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e86\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2t)+5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-12\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3t)\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
